Does the fidelity budget transfer? configuration ariel

63 shared shift cases, six pipelines = 2 model families x 3 representations.
Spearman correlation of the per-case accuracy loss, every pair of pipelines.

pipeline A  pipeline B  relationship              rho
norm_xgb    pca_xgb     same model family       0.956
norm_rf     pca_rf      same model family       0.950
pca_xgb     raw_xgb     same model family       0.926
norm_xgb    raw_xgb     same model family       0.902
pca_rf      raw_rf      same model family       0.790
norm_rf     raw_rf      same model family       0.751
norm_xgb    norm_rf     same representation     0.989
pca_xgb     pca_rf      same representation     0.989
raw_xgb     raw_rf      same representation     0.837
norm_rf     pca_xgb     sharing neither         0.961
norm_xgb    pca_rf      sharing neither         0.947
pca_rf      raw_xgb     sharing neither         0.932
norm_rf     raw_xgb     sharing neither         0.924
pca_xgb     raw_rf      sharing neither         0.775
norm_xgb    raw_rf      sharing neither         0.731

physical proxy: Spearman(loss, surviving feature amplitude) = -0.007 (n = 63), so the ordering is not simply how much signal is left.

same representation    n=3  mean rho 0.938   range 0.837-0.989
same model family      n=6  mean rho 0.879   range 0.751-0.956
sharing neither        n=6  mean rho 0.878   range 0.731-0.961

same representation vs all other pairs:   Mann-Whitney U one-sided p = 0.0901   (n = 3 vs 12)
same representation vs same model family: Mann-Whitney U one-sided p = 0.1310
                                         permutation (20k) p = 0.2134
                                         mean difference = +0.059


Magnitude spread on the 32 cases costing at least 5 points to some pipeline:
  the same shift costs a median 6.4x more for one pipeline than another (max 101x).
  Between the two strongest pipelines alone it reaches 39.0x.

No ranking inversion under haze 3e7: frozen 96.47 -> 90.35%, PCA 92.09 -> 85.54%;
the in-domain ranking holds under the shift on this grid.

Sharing a model family agrees no better than sharing nothing (0.879 vs 0.878);
the representation is what carries the budget.
